---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../../assets/ashmit-portrait.png';
import { affiliation, researchQuestion } from '../data/profile';
---
<Layout>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="introduction" id="about">
      <div id="background">
        <p class="affiliation">{affiliation} · Class of 2027</p>
        <h1>Ashmit Mukherjee</h1>
        <p>{researchQuestion} I want to study this in a computer science PhD starting in fall 2027.</p>
      </div>
      <Image class="portrait" src={portrait} alt="Ashmit Mukherjee" width={128} height={128} densities={[1, 2, 3]} format="webp" loading="eager" />
    </header>

    <section class="home-section" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-heading">
      <h2 id="research-heading">Group decisions and AI</h2>
      <p class="research-bridge">In the lab, I study how people make decisions with advice from AI. In my capstone, I give models the rules of a game and ask them to predict how human groups will do.</p>
      <article class="research-entry">
        <h3><a href="/work/human-ai-collaboration/">AI advice and cooperation</a></h3>
        <p>I built the Social Dynamics Lab’s experiment platform and lead its development. Each player can get private advice from a language model. We can vary whether the advisers talk to each other first and see what each player was told before they made their move.</p>
        <p class="byline">NYU Abu Dhabi faculty mentors · Professors <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=GAxIreYAAAAJ">Benjamin Rosche</a> and <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=9lTiKjwAAAAJ">Hanan Salam</a></p>
      </article>
      <article class="research-entry">
        <h3><a href="/work/synthetic-pilot-lab/">Forecasting the effect of punishment on group earnings</a></h3>
        <p>Would groups earn more if players could punish each other? Claude Haiku 4.5 and the human experts both expected a small gain. Across the 20 game designs, groups actually earned less on average with punishment. The original study’s regression made more accurate forecasts than either.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="ebrain-heading">
      <h2 id="ebrain-heading">Protein models and scientific literature</h2>
      <article class="research-entry" id="manuscript">
        <h3><a href="/work/protein-language-models/">Bio-LoRA for protein language models</a></h3>
        <p>At the eBRAIN Lab, I wrote the training and evaluation code for identifying signal peptides and predicting where they are cut. I’m a co-first author of Bio-LoRA, our manuscript on using amino-acid chemistry to initialize protein models.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="research-entry">
        <h3><a href="/work/biosynthesis-paper-database/">Biosynthesis paper database</a></h3>
        <p>My pipeline collected 139,011 paper records for a study of how AI systems retrieve methods from the biosynthesis literature. About a third lacked abstracts. The lipid search also pulled in papers on cell signaling, a different question from how cells make lipids.</p>
        <p class="byline">Led by <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=USe518cAAAAJ">Minghao Shao</a>, with faculty lead Professor <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=xSR276UAAAAJ">Muhammad Shafique</a></p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-heading">
      <div class="section-heading" id="experience"><h2 id="projects-heading">Software and competitions</h2><a href="/work/">All projects</a></div>
      <p>My team, SegfaultObservers, took first place in the MENA region at the <a href="/work/csaw-llm-ctf/">CSAW LLM CTF Attack Competition</a>. I ran six agents in parallel and built the verifier we used to check their solutions.</p>
      <p>With <a href="/work/fieldlens/">FieldLens</a>, I tested whether a local model could answer questions about a vehicle incident and show the camera or GPS records behind its answer. For <a href="/work/roomwise/">RoomWise</a>, I connected furniture listings to a room preview so shoppers can see how each chair fits as they swipe.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
